# Everything listed here is kept OUT of the build context, so it can
# never end up in an image layer. Two reasons a path appears below:
# (1) it's a secret, (2) it's host state that compose bind-mounts in at
# runtime, so baking a stale copy into the image would be wrong.

# --- Secrets: must NEVER be baked into a layer ---
# GEMINI_API_KEY is injected at runtime via compose's `env_file: .env`.
# Image layers are readable by anyone who can pull the image, and
# deleting a file in a later layer does not remove it from the earlier
# one -- so the only safe handling is to never copy it in at all.
.env
.env.*
!env.example

# --- Host state: bind-mounted at runtime, see compose.yaml ---
data/
storage/
logs/

# --- Virtual environments ---
# The image builds its own venv via `uv sync`; a host .venv is both huge
# and platform-wrong (Windows binaries in a Linux image).
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Python bytecode / build artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- Model caches (multi-GB, re-downloaded into the mounted storage/) ---
.cache/
models/
*.bin
*.safetensors

# --- Dev-only: not needed at runtime ---
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Version control ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Docs and agent config ---
# README.md is force-included below: pyproject.toml declares
# `readme = "README.md"`, so uv needs it present during `uv sync`.
*.md
!README.md
.claude/
.claudeignore

# --- Docker's own files: nothing in the image needs them ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yaml
docker-compose.yaml
